development.question_text:
Solve $2x+6\le10$ and show the solution on the number line.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-2.9,0)--(2.9,0);
\foreach \v in {-5,...,5} {\draw (0.5*\v,0.12)--(0.5*\v,-0.12); \node[below] at (0.5*\v,-0.16) {$\v$};}
\node[right] at (3,0) {$x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.solution_text:
$2x+6\le10$
$2x\le4$
$x\le2$
$\le$ includes $2$, so the circle is closed and the arrow points left.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-2.9,0)--(2.9,0);
\foreach \v in {-5,...,5} {\draw (0.5*\v,0.12)--(0.5*\v,-0.12); \node[below] at (0.5*\v,-0.16) {$\v$};}
\draw[very thick,-{Stealth}] (1,0)--(-2.7,0);
\fill (1,0) circle (2.4pt);
\node[right] at (3,0) {$x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.question_text:
Solve $7-2x<9$ and show the solution on the number line.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-2.9,0)--(2.9,0);
\foreach \v in {-5,...,5} {\draw (0.5*\v,0.12)--(0.5*\v,-0.12); \node[below] at (0.5*\v,-0.16) {$\v$};}
\node[right] at (3,0) {$x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.solution_text:
$7-2x<9$
$-2x<2$
$x>-1$, after dividing both sides by $-2$ and reversing the symbol
$>$ leaves $-1$ out, so the circle is open and the arrow points right.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-2.9,0)--(2.9,0);
\foreach \v in {-5,...,5} {\draw (0.5*\v,0.12)--(0.5*\v,-0.12); \node[below] at (0.5*\v,-0.16) {$\v$};}
\draw[very thick,-{Stealth}] (-0.5,0)--(2.7,0);
\draw[fill=white] (-0.5,0) circle (2.4pt);
\node[right] at (3,0) {$x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

mastery.solution_text:
$-x\ge5$
$x\le-5$, after dividing both sides by $-1$ and reversing the symbol
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-4.4,0)--(1.4,0);
\foreach \v in {-8,...,2} {\draw (0.5*\v,0.12)--(0.5*\v,-0.12); \node[below] at (0.5*\v,-0.16) {$\v$};}
\draw[very thick,-{Stealth}] (-2.5,0)--(-4.2,0);
\fill (-2.5,0) circle (2.4pt);
\node[right] at (1.5,0) {$x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$x\ge-5$ needs no work and shades the other side of the same boundary.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-4.4,0)--(1.4,0);
\foreach \v in {-8,...,2} {\draw (0.5*\v,0.12)--(0.5*\v,-0.12); \node[below] at (0.5*\v,-0.16) {$\v$};}
\draw[very thick,-{Stealth}] (-2.5,0)--(1.2,0);
\fill (-2.5,0) circle (2.4pt);
\node[right] at (1.5,0) {$x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Dividing by $-1$ reverses the symbol, so the two solution sets point in opposite directions and share only $x=-5$.
